          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Peano arithmetic refers to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory"} theory
            which formalizes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic"} arithmetic
            operations on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            and their properties. There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order
            Peano arithmetic and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second-order+logic"} second-order
            Peano arithmetic, and one may speak of Peano arithmetic in higher-order type theory.
          %p
            As first-order logic has certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntactic
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+theory"} model-theoretic
            advantages over second-order logic, and has been much further developed, the default notion of Peano arithmetic is usually taken to be the first-order one. However, we will describe both the first- and second-order notions. Note that Peano’s original treatment was second-order.
          %h2#secondorder_peano_arithmetic Second-order Peano arithmetic
          %p
            Against a fixed background of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"}> sets
            ” (which we consider
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} categorically
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            with an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo :
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0: 1 \to N
            and an unary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo :
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s: N \to N
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∀
                        %mi x
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_x \neg s(x) = 0
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∀
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_{x, y} s(x) = s(y) \Rightarrow x = y
                ;
            %li
              %p
                (Second-order
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∀
                          %mrow
                            %mi I
                            %mo ⊆
                            %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mo ∀
                          %mi x
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mi s
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mi I
                        %mo =
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_{I \subseteq N} [0 \in I \wedge (\forall_x x \in I \Rightarrow s(x) \in I)] \Rightarrow I = N
          %p
            Regarding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+an+endofunctor"} algebra of an endofunctor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
